    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0510" n="1244" xml:id="pg1244"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 511.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your No.
                    414, of the 8th instant, regarding the visit of the <hi rendition="#italic">San
                        Francisco</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> to Turkish
                    waters. The arrival of the former at Sagua was attended with the usual
                    courtesies, and must tend to promote cordial relations.</p>
                <p>I answered the inquiry of the Porte on the subject that the visit of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">San Francisco</hi> was a friendly one, but such vessels
                    were designed for the protection of American interests.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
